8. Create required directories for the patches and install.


[root@caoradbauto01 ~] mkdir /u01
[root@caoradbauto01 ~] chown oracle:oinstall /u01


[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oraInventory
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/logs
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/keystore
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/patches 


*****************************************************************************************************************
Download Latest Release Update
*****************************************************************************************************************
9. Oracle released RU 19.32 in July 2026, and we will proceed with the RECOMMENDED download option from OTN. This ensures that all compatible and available patches for the release are included.
Release Updates and associated patches can be downloaded using Oracle’s AutoUpgrade utility. To enable this, the latest autoupgrade.jar must be downloaded from Oracle. The steps for doing so are provided below.

(a). Download latest AutoUpdate.jar file

  Using Curl :
  
				 wget https://download.oracle.com/otn-pub/otn_software/autoupgrade.jar
  
  Using wget :
		
				 wget https://download.oracle.com/otn-pub/otn_software/autoupgrade.jar
				 
  From MOS Note: KB123450
  
  From https://www.oracle.com/database/upgrades/				

  
  Using autoupgrade config file :
  
			Config File : get-patches.cfg
			
			global.global_log_dir=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/logs
			global.keystore=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/keystore
			global.folder=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/patches

			patch1.platform=LINUX.X64
			patch1.target_version=19
			patch1.patch=AU
			
# The challenge with this method is that it requires an existing autoupgrade.jar to execute the command. This configuration is primarily intended for downloading the most recent autoupgrade.jar. It is useful when your system is running an older AutoUpgrade version and you need to refresh it with the latest one. When using the RECOMMENDED patch download option, AutoUpgrade will automatically retrieve the latest AU version.
			

10. In order to download patches from MyOracleSupport using AutoUpgrade we need to Store our MOS Credentials in AutoUpgrade Keystore. Below are the instructions to create keystore.

***************************************************************************************************************************
Create Autoupgrade Keystore
****************************************************************************************************************************

# Create a config file to download patches which has keystore folder location too

vi get-patches.cfg
global.global_log_dir=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/logs
global.keystore=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/keystore
global.folder=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/patches

patch1.platform=LINUX.X64
patch1.target_version=19
patch1.patch=RECOMMENDED,JDK

# Run the below command to load password
[oracle@caoradboel10 software]$ java -jar autoupgrade.jar -config get-patches.cfg -patch -load_password
Processing config file ...

Starting AutoUpgrade Patching Password Loader - Type help for available options
Creating new AutoUpgrade Patching keystore - Password required
Enter password:
Enter password again:
AutoUpgrade Patching keystore was successfully created

# Add MOS Credentails to the Keystore.

MOS> add -user <MOS Username/Email Address>
