*************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
																				Install Oracle DB Home 
*************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

12. Install Oracle DB Home 
# Now that the software has been downloaded, I will copy it to the /u01/app/oracle/software directory, which is the location referenced in the configuration file.
You can also update your config file to point directly to the folder where the patches were downloaded.

(a). Create a AutoUprade config file to install software.

vi install-home.cfg

global.global_log_dir=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/logs
install1.patch=RU:19.32,OPATCH,OJVM,JDK,DPBP
install1.folder=/u01/app/oracle/software
install1.target_home=/u01/app/19.32.0/db
install1.home_settings.oracle_base=/u01/app/oracle
install1.home_settings.edition=EE
install1.home_settings.inventory_location=/u01/app/oraInventory
install1.download=no


(b). Below command will run the install as a job in the background while opening the console to run few usefule commands like status of the jobs and tasks

